  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Details\n\nCurrently, there is no way to listen to the *arbitrary* entry of a station by a player. This results in additional overhead and workload, requiring an Udon behaviour on every station which needs to respond to this event, which both risks performance decreases and generates undue developer workload in worst-case scenarios.\n\n# Feature Request\n\nProvide `OnPlayerStationEntered(VRCPlayerApi player, VRCStation station)` and `OnPlayerStationExited(VRCPlayerApi player, VRCStation station)` as global events which can be listened to via udon.\n\nSimilar to other `OnPlayer` events, these would be triggered by the player's actions/state, as opposed to any particular event on a particular object. By this method, developers, when needed, can work with stations *arbitrarily*, such as for setting the height of a station based on a slider, manipulating arbitrary station properties, and working with stations in a complex manner from a singular Udon behaviour, whilst avoiding duplicate code, scripts, or messy distributed script setups.",
